Latency = cycles from START accepted to DONE (= CYCLES register). Formula of sc_tpu_ctrl.v
(CALCULATION): CYCLES = (64/IL + 16/IL) * (NL*IL/4 + 1 + 2^K) + 2*(NL + 3), NL = 16.
For IL = 8 the formula is confirmed by SIMULATION (tb_sc_tpu D8 and every golden vector:
CYCLES register == measured BUSY cycles == formula; logs/tpu/tb_sc_tpu_mode*.log).
IL = 4 / 16 latencies are CALCULATION only (not simulated: the golden vectors are defined
for IL = 8 only). Time per inference at 27 MHz, K = 8: IL4 203.6 us, IL8 108.4 us, IL16 60.9 us.

LUT4 counts every occupied LUT position (LUT1..4 cells + ALU cells + 8 per RAM16SDP4,
requirements/BUDGETS.md); 'max util %' is the highest of LUT4/ALU/DFF/RAM16SDP4/BSRAM/MUX2_LUT5
(85 % rule of ARCHITECTURE.md 10). BSRAM = 1 SDPX9B (weight RAM); RAM16SDP4 = INPUT + BIAS.

